source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: A backslash before a `|` in the visible text protects nothing: the split leaves a target Jira cannot resolve and it renders an error span, which jiro reproduces as a link to that target.
-- input.jira --
[a\|b|http://x]
-- rendered.html --
<p><span class="error">&#91;a\|b|http://x&#93;</span></p>
-- want.md --
:link[a\\\\]{target="b|http://x"}
-- warnings.json --
[]
